---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { PHONE, PHONE_TEL } from '../../../lib/site.ts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Foundation concerns before listing or during the inspection period"
  description="Independent foundation measurement for Arizona real estate transactions — before listing or during the buyer’s inspection period. Not a formal real-estate inspection."
>
  <div class="container">
    <h1 class="page-title">Foundation concerns before listing or during the inspection period</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Foundation issues surface at two high-stakes moments in a real estate transaction: before the house is listed, and during the buyer’s inspection period.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>Before listing</h2>
      <p>
        A clear independent read helps a seller decide whether to repair, disclose and price accordingly, or simply document the condition. Surprises after the listing goes live are more expensive.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>During the inspection period</h2>
      <p>
        A second opinion can keep a deal from collapsing under a large repair bid that no one fully understands. The goal is not to kill the transaction or to force a repair. It is to replace fear with measured information so both sides can decide on facts.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What this is (and is not)</h2>
      <p>
        This is not a formal real-estate inspection product. It is a practical conversation and measurement when foundation concerns appear. Realtors can recommend it as a calm, paid, independent measurement step when foundation concerns appear — without choosing sides between repair companies. Agents in the White Mountains and across Arizona use it as a low-drama resource for clients who need clarity without another sales process.
      </p>
      <div class="contact-box">
        <p><strong>Realtors and homeowners — call or text</strong></p>
        <a class="phone-link" href={`tel:${PHONE_TEL}`}>{PHONE}</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
